{
  "dom_id": "step-e4716",
  "name": "Example: Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix",
  "problem": "Is \n$\\begin{aligned}E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}$ \nan elementary matrix?",
  "worked_solution": "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation.\n\nThe given matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I_2$ by applying the elementary row operation $R_2:= R_2+(-5) R_1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
